<title>HUNGARY: Egis confirms buy of Polish drugs company.</title>
<headline>Egis confirms buy of Polish drugs company.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian pharmaceuticals company Egis Gyogyszergyar Rt confirmed on Friday earlier press reports that Egis and its French owner Servier S.A. bought a Polish pharmaceuticals company.</p>
<p>&quot;Egis buys a minority stake in the (Polish) company...and Servier S.A. acquires a majority stake,&quot; Egis said in a statement in the official bourse gazette.</p>
<p>It did not name the Polish company. Newspaper reports on Thursday said the company had sales last year amounting to around $5 million and had a strong market position in generic products.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
